+## Discovering Skills from Other Agents' Directories
+
+Other coding agents — Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, and Cursor — use the same `SKILL.md` layout, so a skill written for them usually works in OpenHands unchanged. Enable `load_compatible_skills` to also discover those native directories:
+
+| Scope | Directories scanned (in addition to the OpenHands locations) |
+|---|---|
+| User | `~/.claude/skills/`, `~/.codex/skills/`, `~/.gemini/skills/`, `~/.cursor/skills/` |
+| Project | `<workspace>/.claude/skills/`, `<workspace>/.codex/skills/`, `<workspace>/.gemini/skills/`, `<workspace>/.cursor/skills/` |
+
+```python icon="python" focus={2}
+agent_context = AgentContext(
+    load_compatible_skills=True,  # Also scan .claude/.codex/.gemini/.cursor skill dirs
+    load_user_skills=True,        # Extend the user scope
+    load_project_skills=True,     # Extend the project scope
+)
+```
+
+Enabling `load_compatible_skills` also turns on the user and project scopes, because the vendor directories only extend those scopes — there is no way to scan a vendor directory without also scanning the OpenHands locations in the same scope. Within a scope, every OpenHands source wins over the vendor directories: `.agents/skills/` beats `.claude/skills/`, and an installed OpenHands skill beats a vendor skill of the same name in the user scope. Only `SKILL.md` skills are read from the vendor directories, so loose Markdown notes there are ignored.
+
+The vendor directories are **additive and lower precedence**: a skill name that exists in both `.agents/skills/` and `.claude/skills/` resolves to the `.agents/skills/` version. Nothing changes when the setting is off, so this is safe to leave disabled.
+
+<Note>
+ACP agents (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI) read their own native skill directories from the session working directory. OpenHands clears `load_compatible_skills` and `load_project_skills` for ACP agents so that content is not loaded twice.
+</Note>
+
 ## Loading Public Skills
 
 OpenHands maintains a [public skills repository](https://github.com/OpenHands/extensions) with community-contributed skills. You can automatically load these skills without waiting for SDK updates.
